From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: X670 Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
Date: Sun, 02 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vndk: drop device-local libbinder-v32 prebuilt

hardware/lineage/compat also ships a vendor libbinder-v32 prebuilt, so
defining it here collides with it at build time:

  MODULE.TARGET.SHARED_LIBRARIES.libbinder-v32 already defined by
  hardware/lineage/compat

Drop the device-local module; libbinder-v32 is still provided by
hardware/lineage/compat when present (vendorsetup.sh only applies this
patch in that case). Keep libssl-v33 as-is.

Change-Id: I11111f0b657a47a19f8e07cee31db2fd5f4c5555
---
 vndk/Android.bp | 15 ---------------
 1 file changed, 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vndk/Android.bp b/vndk/Android.bp
index 725de72..bf6ec70 100644
--- a/vndk/Android.bp
+++ b/vndk/Android.bp
@@ -1,18 +1,3 @@
-cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
-    name: "libbinder-v32",
-    vendor: true,
-    strip: {
-        none: true,
-    },
-    target: {
-        android_arm64: {
-            srcs: ["v32/arm64/libbinder-v32.so"],
-        },
-    },
-    compile_multilib: "64",
-    check_elf_files: false,
-}
-
 cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
     name: "libssl-v33",
     vendor: true,
-- 
2.53.0
